From 77f30d1e6e2a582d807ba5a3f1040f817e4d14d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:54:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] gts4lv-common: Override kernel BPF version

Android 16 mainline modules (netd, Tethering, bpfloader) expect eBPF
features from Linux 5.4. LineageOS 23.x only supports older kernels that
carry 1:1 eBPF backports making them feature-equivalent to
android12-5.4, and then advertises that via ro.bpf.kver_override.

DO NOT apply this until kernel/samsung/sdm670 carries the complete
eBPF backport series and passes netd_integration_test; overriding the
version on an un-backported 4.9 kernel makes bpfloader/netd fail and the
device will not boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 product.prop | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/product.prop b/product.prop
index a9871d5..6cb01dd 100644
--- a/product.prop
+++ b/product.prop
@@ -8,3 +8,6 @@ ro.lmk.downgrade_pressure=100
 ro.lmk.kill_heaviest_task=true
 ro.lmk.kill_timeout_ms=100
 ro.lmk.use_minfree_levels=true
+
+# eBPF
+ro.bpf.kver_override=5.4.299
-- 
2.43.0

